# External MCP edits visible in the Agent panel: verification note (2026-10-21)

Working note, untracked. Do not commit.

Landed as one commit, 5a1484fc74 on local jusprin-newui (not pushed). It shows an external MCP tool's edits in the Agent panel when no agent is set up, names the MCP client on change rows, and adds the "Set up the agent" bar with the shrink animation. The work was done in `.claude/worktrees/mcp-external-edits` (branch `claude/mcp-external-edits-visible`, squashed onto c4004fd984).

## Verified
- Agent page Vitest: 579 passed, styles.test.ts included. Before the fix, the new App tests failed: the "No agent connected" offer replaced the thread.
- agent_bridge_tests: 402 cases passed. This run was before the rebase; upstream's two new commits touch no C++ that suite covers. The new bridge test fails without the bridge change: the edit was named "jusprin-mcp", the bridge's own name.
- brand_tokens_tests: passed after the rebase. The two "failed as expected" are tests built to fail.
- Claude Code 2.1.283 sends `clientInfo {"name":"claude-code","title":"Claude Code"}` at initialize. Captured with a stub stdio server under a throwaway HOME (`claude mcp list`, no model calls).
- Browser check of the built page with a scripted fake host, in light and dark:
  - The empty chat shows the offer.
  - When an external change arrives, the offer shrinks into the bar. A frame was captured paused mid-animation.
  - The final state shows the setup card "Edited by Claude Code", the row "Wall loops 2 → 3 · Claude Code, in …", the slice card, and the bar.

- shell_theme_tests: passed (349 assertions).
- Live app end to end, macOS Release build of the same tree:
  - Setup: isolated `--datadir` and HOME, no agent, and the model endpoint pointed at a closed port. The Agent page was the built bundle plus a script that reported what the page showed.
  - A scripted stdio client went through the built `jusprin-mcp`. It said it was `claude-code` / "Claude Code", applied wall loops 2 → 3, and started a slice.

